[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-ayatori-bench-coscientist-iteration-36", :doc/title "ayatori Co-Scientist Iteration 36 — IC07/IC08 top-20 in the query; the planner's per-version recount closed; sf1-full 2115 / 3512 ops/s", :doc/path "bench/coscientist-iteration-36.edn", :doc/body "# Co-Scientist iteration 36 - IC07/IC08 top-20 inside the query, and two write-side stalls found and closed\n\n> Seed: iteration 35's S27. Judge: bench/benchmark.edn v2; rung :sf1-full;\n> SUT levi -Xmx10g, driver judah, LAN; impl :datalog.\n\n## Generate\n\n  IC07 and IC08 sorted in the harness after a full join, so the grouped\n  drive could not take them. Now `:order-by`/`:limit` are in the query:\n  IC08's driver is the reply's creationDate with group `[?reply replyOf\n  ?msg]` over the person's messages; IC07's is like/creationDate with\n  group `[?like like/message ?msg]` -- and because one row per liker is\n  not a query clause, N starts at 20 and doubles while N rows hold fewer\n  than 20 distinct likers and the query was not exhausted.\n\n  Prediction, written first: IC07 16.8 -> a few ms; IC08's p95 tightens;\n  both ceilings rise.\n\n## Rank\n\n  Gate 1,082/0 with three group orders built at startup. Then the first\n  8-slot sweep FAILED at 640 reads where iteration 35 had passed -- with\n  IC08/IS7/IS2 p95 at 96/101/79 ms and IC02 at 0.6. An isolate (those four\n  ops at 400/s, with and without the stream) put it on the stream, and on\n  exactly the ops whose queries carry an all-open clause on an attribute\n  the stream writes. The planner's `[nil attr nil]` estimate was an exact\n  datom count cached by IDENTITY of the attribute's :aevt map (iteration\n  20's fix for 9 ms of planning); every insert on the attribute replaced\n  that map, so nearly every plan under the stream recounted 2-3M buckets.\n  IC02's creationDate clause is a fused range, not that shape -- which is\n  why it never showed. The estimate is now the subject count: O(1), no\n  cache, nothing to go stale.\n\n    isolate, 400 reads/s + stream    ic08 p95   is7 p95   is2 p95   on-time\n      recount cache                    96.6      101.0     78.6      73.2%\n      subject count                     1.4        0.5      0.7     100.0%\n\n  A second, smaller one: each order version was a 1,024-element vector\n  rebuilt through a lazy seq per push, 3-4 pushes per insert. Now a\n  conj/trim ring (datalog 3ab273e4).\n\n    rung sf1-full  slots  reads/s  tcr      upd/s  on-time%  thru/s\n      it.35           8     640    0.0002   1092    100.00   1730.8\n      it.36           8    1024    0.0002   1092    100.00   2115.4   (1280: 64.9% fails)\n      it.35          32     512    0.00015  1475    100.00   1984.8\n      it.36          32    2048    0.00015  1475    100.00   3512.2   (2560: 51.5% fails)\n\n  Wire p50 at 8 slots / 1024: ic07 8.6, ic09 13.1, is3 8.2, everything\n  else 2.0-2.4 ms (the LAN hop is ~2 ms). Read-after-write 600/0/0.\n  Tests: datalog JVM 135/418/0, cljs 139/429/0; kotobase-peer 262/803/0.\n\n## Reflect\n\n  - The prediction held for IC07/IC08 but the row would have been a\n    regression without the isolate: a sweep that fails where the last one\n    passed is a finding, not noise, and the four-op/two-mode isolate cost\n    two minutes. Iteration 20's cache was right for a read-only SUT and\n    wrong the day the SUT wrote; the receipt of iteration 20 said what it\n    measured, and the writes came ten iterations later.\n  - The full SF1 column now stands at 2115 / 3512 against the subset\n    column's 2333 / 4546 -- the 15x larger data costs 1.3x at 32 slots.\n  - Left on this rung: IC09 (13 ms, two-hop over hundreds of groups),\n    IC07's fetch-more loop (6 ms), and GC pauses of 60-170 ms max even\n    without the stream (a ZGC trial is a one-flag experiment).\n\n## Meta\n\nVerdict under bench/benchmark.edn v2: GROWTH (same rung, same mix; 8-slot\nceiling 640 -> 1024, 32-slot 512 -> 2048). Ratio to the audited No.1: 40.\n\nSeeds for iteration 37, in order:\n\n  - ZGC on the SUT (one flag; measure max and p99 under the stream).\n  - S28: IC09 at full scale (13 ms; the two-hop group set).\n  - S26: a full-data parameter set.\n  - S23b: IC05 so INS5 has a covering read.\n  - M3: SF3 (~13 GB) -- persisted plane or a larger host.\n"}]
